  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis_humilis_and_close_relatives_from_guinea_1_pelvicachromis_humilis_liberia_red_en/",
      "html": "<p>The current import from Guinea contains five different species/morphs of the relationship of Pelvicachromis humilis. They all have in common that the males can reach a maximum length of 12 cm. Females always stay smaller.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis_humilis_and_close_relatives_from_guinea_1_pelvicachromis_humilis_liberia_red_en/",
      "html": "<p>Pelvicachromis humilis \"Liberia Red\" was collected, as can be seen from the name, in the border region between Liberia and Guinea. The fish known in the hobby in the 1990s under the name Pelvicachromis humilis \"Liberia Red\" seems to represent another, different variety/species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25c-perchlike-fishes-3-remaining-cichlids-from-africa/pelvicachromis_humilis_and_close_relatives_from_guinea_1_pelvicachromis_humilis_liberia_red_en/",
      "html": "<p>The females are the more colorful animals; there is always a clearly marked sexual dichromatism. During mating and displaying the colours change drastically: the fish seem to glow from inside in these situations. In males of the current import there is a red pattern in the caudal fin. The remaining coloration differs a lot, depending on the mood. The bright shining zone on the belly of the female, which is present in all forms of the P. humilis relationship, is expressed very intensively in Pelvicachromis humilis \"Liberia Red\".</p>"
    }
  ],
